Title:
NoNameAx (NaX) — Position-Independent C2 Beacon for Adaptix Framework

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
- NaX is an Adaptix-compatible Windows x64 C2 agent consisting of a position-independent (PIC) shellcode beacon, a Stardust-pattern UDRL loader, and Go-based server/agent plugins.  
- It focuses on stealthy in-memory execution via module stomping (image-backed memory) rather than private RWX allocations, and includes clean unwind metadata handling (.pdata/.xdata) to support stack walking.  
- The beacon resolves APIs via PEB walking (no imports/CRT), supports malleable C2 profiles with runtime switching, and uses WinHTTP (proxy-aware) plus SMB transport.  
- It implements evasion primitives like DLL load notification callback removal (LdrRegisterDllNotification unhooking) and a BeaconGate + sleepmask mechanism that proxies sleep/wait APIs through a module-stomped BOF.  
- Post-exploitation features include in-process BOF execution (COFF loader), token theft/impersonation/creation, SOCKS and port-forward tunneling, SMB pivoting, and common file/process commands.  
- Useful primarily for red teams/pentesters and security researchers building or studying modern beacon tradecraft and EDR telemetry reduction techniques.

Technical Focus:
- PIC shellcode beacon design (PEB walk, hashed API resolution, no imports/CRT)
- Module stomping (image-backed execution, LDR entry patching, sacrificial DLL selection)
- Unwind metadata / stack-walk correctness (.pdata/.xdata injection)
- CFG-aware execution (SetProcessValidCallTargets allowlisting)
- Malleable C2 profiles and transform pipelines (headers/cookies/params, XOR/base64/hex)
- BOF execution and sleepmask/BeaconGate API proxying

Use Cases:
- Build an Adaptix C2 agent with stealthier memory characteristics (IMG-backed vs PRV)
- Execute BOFs in-process with module-stomped code sections and unwind support
- Implement/experiment with sleep obfuscation via BeaconGate + custom sleepmask BOFs
- Operate through enterprise proxies using WinHTTP auto proxy detection (PAC/WPAD)
- Pivot and tunnel traffic (SOCKS4/5, local/reverse port forwards) over HTTP/SMB
- Research/detect techniques like DLL notification callback removal and CFG bypass patterns

Keywords:
Adaptix Framework, C2 beacon, PIC shellcode, PEB walk, FNV1a hashing, module stomping, sacrificial DLL, image-backed memory, .pdata, .xdata, unwind info, clean stack walk, Control Flow Guard, SetProcessValidCallTargets, WinHTTP, PAC, WPAD, SMB pivoting, BOF, COFF loader, sleepmask, BeaconGate, LdrRegisterDllNotification, token impersonation, AES-128-CBC, BCrypt, SOCKS proxy, port forwarding, Stardust, UDRL loader